 his destroyer.\n Śambara cast the child into the roaring sea, and a large fish swallowed\n it. This fish was caught by a fisherman and taken to the demon; and when\n it was cut up, a beautiful child came out from the belly, and Māyāvatī,\n the mistress of Śambaraʼs household, at the desire of Nārada, carefully\n reared him from childhood. As he grew up, she was fascinated by the beauty\n of his person, but Pradyumna reproved her for entertaining towards himself\n feelings so unbecoming a mother as he considered her. But when he was\n told that he was not her son, but of Viṣṇu and was cast into the sea\n by Śambara, he became enraged, and, challenging him to fight, succeeded\n in killing him by the force of illusions. He and Māyāvatī afterwards\n repaired to the house of Kṛṣṇa, where Nārada told him and Rukmiṇī\n that the boy was their own and that Māyāvatī was his wife.]"}]}]}],"pradyumnakaH":[{"id":"pradyumnakaH","headword":"प्रद्युम्नकः","headword_slp1":"pradyumnakaH","senses_r":[{"n":1,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"N. of the god of love; Bhāg."}]}]}],"pradraRaka":[{"id":"pradrARaka","headword":"प्रद्राणक","headword_slp1":"pradrARaka","senses_r":[{"n":1,"pos":"a.","spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"Sorely distressed, hard pressed, indigent, poor;\n चाक्रायण इभ्यग्रामे प्रद्राणक उवास Ch. "},{"t":"cite","s":"Up. 1. 10. 1","q":"Up"},{"t":"txt","s":"."}]}]}],"pradru":[{"id":"pradru","headword":"प्रद्रु","headword_slp1":"pradru","senses_r":[{"n":1,"subs":[{"n":"1","spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"To run, run away, retreat or fly to (with acc. or abl.); रणात् प्रद्रवन्ति\n बलानि "},{"t":"cite","s":"Ve. 4","q":""},{"t":"txt","s":"; "},{"t":"cite","s":"Bk. 15. 79","q":"Bk"},{"t":"txt","s":"."}]},{"n":"2","spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"To hasten away, rush towards."}]},{"n":"3","spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"To assail, fall upon, attack."}]},{"n":"4","spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"To attain. ━Caus. To put to flight, rout."}]}],"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"€1 P."}]}]}],"pradrava":[{"id":"pradrava","headword":"प्रद्रव